
Integer coefficients for the element routines in this addon.


Base functions (shape functions)
--------------------------------

See file addons/README_basefunctions


List of the coefficients
------------------------

  1-150: reserved for stokes & viscoelastic add-ons
151-200: reserved for diffuse-interface add-on
201-250: reserved for inertia add-on
251-300: reserved for generalized Stokes add-on
301-350: reserved for compressible fluid add-on
351-400: reserved for deformation fields add-on

401 Time integration scheme for the convection-diffusion-reaction equation:
    0: default (=1)
    1: first-order implicit Euler
    2: second-order implicit Gear (BDF2)

402 q interpolation (base function)
    for a triangle / tetrahedron
      2: P1  
      6: P2
    for a quadrilateral / hexahedron
      4: Q1  
      8: Q2
    for a prism
     15: P1Q1  
     16: P2Q2
    for a pyramid
     17: Q1P1r
     18: Q2P2r

403  Method (method) for spatial discretization:
     0: standard Galerkin
     1: SUPG

404 include the diffusion term in the matrix (-alpha nabla^2 c)
    0: no
    1: yes (with alpha given in coefficients%r(353))

405 include the self-dependent source term in the matrix (beta c)
    0: no
    1: yes (with beta given in coefficients%r(354))

406 choice for the RHS source term f
    0: f equals zero
    1: f constant (and given in coefficients%r(355))
    2: f given by a function of position, funcnr=coefficient%i(407) 
       NOTE: a function must be assigned to coefficients%func1(2)%p
    3: f supplied in the nodes in oldvectors%v(2)
    4: f supplied in the integration points oldvectors%e(2)

407 function number in case the RHS source term f is given by a function

**** parameters 408 and 410 determine how the tau parameter
     of the SUPG method is computed

408 htype, the type of h computation:
        0: take default value (=2)
        1: the standard velocity projection
        2: mapping of the reference element
        3: determined by the size of the element:
           2D: h = (elementsize)**0.5
           3D: h = (elementsize)**1/3
           hence: h is a constant per element
    
409: Reserved for future use. Set to zero for future compatibility.

410 Uscaling, how is the U scaling computed:
        0: take default value (=3)
        1: |u| in the center of the element only
        2: 1/N sum_i |u|_i , i=1,..,N with N the number of integration points.
        3: |u| in the integration points separately
        4: global scaling Uglobal = coefficient%r(357)

411 choice for the beta term in SUPG
    0: beta = 0
    1: beta = 1
    2: beta = 0            if Peh < 1
       beta = 1 - 1/Peh    if Peh > 1
    3: beta = coth(Peh) - 1/Peh
    4: beta = Peh/3        if Peh < 3
       beta = 1            if Peh > 3
    5: beta = constant (given in coefficients%r(356)
    NOTE: this beta is different from beta coefficient in the equations given
    by coefficients%i(405).

412 Adjust the tau parameter in SUPG for Courant numbers C=U*deltat/h smaller
    than 1:
             { beta*h/2U      for C >= 1
        tau ={
             { beta*deltat/2  for C < 1
    0: no
    1: yes

413 number of right hand sides to assemble. The way in which the RHS is 
    determined depends on the choice for coefficients%i(414).
    NOTE: Only relevant for coefficients%i(413)>1, otherwise a single rhs is 
    assumed with choices given by coefficients%i(406).

414 choice for multiple right-hand sides to assemble (coefficients%i(413)>1):
    0: f equals zero for all RHSs
    1: f constant (and given for the RHS with number n in
       coefficients%ra(2)%a(n)
    2: f given by a function of position with the function number
       for the RHS with number n in coefficients%ra(2)%a(n)
       NOTE:a function must be assigned to coefficients%func1(2)%p
    3: f supplied in the nodes in oldvectors%v1(2)%p(n) for the
       RHS with number n
    4: f supplied in the integration points oldvectors%e(2), where
       the element vector must contain nrsh one-dimensional real
       vectors per element (where nrsh is the number of RHSs to
       assemble (=coefficients%i(413)) )

415-450: Reserved for future use. Set to zero for future compatibility.
